   [campaign]    [soul] ORACLE decision: kind=action ctx={'place': 'You\'re in Fuchsia City — outdoors under open sky (a town with a Pokémon Center and a Mart).. From here: SOUTH → Route 19; EAST → Route 15 — wild Pokémon to catch/train; WEST → Route 18 — wild Pokémon to catch/train. Places you\'ve been with wild Pokémon you can walk back to: Route 14; the Safari Zone; Route 13. You can walk to anywhere you\'ve already been. You have SURF — you can cross water. Field moves ready: STRENGTH.. Okay — to get past this I need Zapdos — the L50 legendary bird inside the Power Plant, across Route 10\'s water strip. The electric answer to Lorelei\'s waters and Lance\'s Gyarados, free for the catching once Surf is taught. Heads up: you have ZERO Poké Balls — you literally can\'t catch a teammate until you buy some at a Mart, so a Mart run has to come before any catching.. HOW POKÉMON WORKS (what you\'re playing for): the GOAL is to earn 8 Gym Badges, beat the Elite Four, and roll the credits — that\'s beating the game. You build a TEAM of up to 6 Pokémon you like AND that cover each other (types/roles) — a solo carry with a dead-weight bench is a losing setup; a real trainer fields a balanced, levelled squad. CATCHING wild Pokémon is central (\'gotta catch \'em all\') — you catch to build that team and to fill the Pokédex. When you meet a wild Pokémon, weigh it: is it cool/strong/useful, does it cover a gap, is it better than a bench-warmer? — keep your best ~6, and build a squad you actually like. THE ARC: build a team -> beat the 8 gyms prepared -> Elite Four -> credits. ALSO NORMAL: you entered your own name (and your rival\'s) when the game began — people in this world knowing your names is ordinary, not a mystery to react to. RIGHT NOW your team is thin/lopsided (a strong lead but weak or too few others) — that\'s why tough trainers wall you. Building up a real squad (catch a good new teammate, level the weak ones) is how a prepared trainer gets past these. THE MAIN QUEST IS A FIXED PATH you\'re always on: beat the 8 Gym Leaders in order, then the Elite Four, then you win the game. All 8 badges are yours — the Elite Four is the final challenge before the credits. Word on the road about the Elite Four: the Elite Four open with an ice-and-water lady — folks say lightning and grass are how you slip past her; and then the dragon master himself — and everyone says the same thing: ice is the only thing a dragon truly fears. YOUR STORY SO FAR (what you\'ve actually done — your past, not the future): All eight Gym Badges are yours. The Elite Four and the Champion are the summit.. Time to pick up my zapdos from Power Plant (static L50 — Surf up the Route 10 water from the east bank). This has been on the plan since the start.. THINGS YOU\'VE HEARD AND READ (from people and signs — your own notes, use them when they point somewhere): "I had a vision of your arrival. I have had psychic powers since I was a child. It started when a spoon I carelessly tossed, bent. I dislike battling, but if you"; "Sealed within that TM06 lies TOXIC! It is a secret technique dating back some four hundred years."; "KIRA put the TM06 in the TM CASE."; "KIRA received TM06 from KOGA.". YOUR PLAN — right now: You\'re ready — stop grinding and push forward to the next objective. Next: FIRST Zapdos — the L50 legendary bird inside the Power Plant, across Route 10\'s water strip. The electric answer to Lorelei\'s waters and Lance\'s Gyarados, free for the catching once Surf is taught — the gym comes right after; that errand is the road. Bigger picture: Take on the Elite Four. Your team right now: blastoise (L67), lapras (L26), fearow (L38), moltres (L50), diglett (L18), abra the kadabra (L19). Remember YOU are the one playing this — narrate your plan to chat in your own voice (first person: "I\'m grinding", "my team"), and never ask anyone what you\'re doing or who\'s on your team — you know.', 'progress': '8 badge(s) earned (Boulder, Cascade, Thunder, Rainbow, Soul, Marsh, Volcano, Earth). All 8 badges earned. Pokédex: 18 caught. All 8 badges — Victory Road and the Elite Four are next. This is the endgame.', 'party': 'blastoise (L67), lapras (L26), fearow (L38), moltres (L50), diglett (L18), abra the kadabra (L19)', 'goal': {'short': "You're ready — stop grinding and push forward to the next objective", 'medium': "FIRST Zapdos — the L50 legendary bird inside the Power Plant, across Route 10's water strip. The electric answer to Lorelei's waters and Lance's Gyarados, free for the catching once Surf is taught — the gym comes right after; that errand is the road", 'long': 'Take on the Elite Four'}, 'strategy': "1) WAR PREP: the Elite Four is five fights with NO Center between them — full restores, revives, ethers, and a levelled WHOLE team, or don't walk in.\n2) TEAM BUILD: zapdos (static) — a LEGENDARY upgrade over any raised electric: L50 on capture, out-levels the whole badge-8 curve. Weaken carefully and BALL it — never KO.\n3) DEX PUSH: 18/50 species caught — at 50 the Route 15 aide (by Fuchsia) hands over the EXP. SHARE (the whole bench levels off every fight). Catch every NEW species you cross; never wander just to hunt.\n4) ICE BEAM FUND: ¥79,878 short of the Game Corner TM13 budget (~¥80,500 total). Ice Beam on the ace freezes everything left — Venusaur, Lance's dragons, the birds. Fight your battles for the payouts, sell loot at marts, buy supplies but never splurge. It arms itself when funded.\n5) STANDING ORDERS: the goal is ROLL CREDITS. Forward progress beats wandering; heal beats fighting hurt; type advantage decides fights; build the planned team, not just the ace."} options=['head_to_league', 'battle', 'stock_up', 'travel:3,8', 'travel:3,5', 'travel:3,1', 'travel:3,3']

